# apps/web build-time configuration. Vite inlines every
# `VITE_*` access at build, so this file documents the
# build-time toggles a contributor needs to set in their
# local `apps/web/.env` (gitignored — same convention as the
# workspace `.env`).

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 1.20b — Web Push subscribe key.
#
# Public half of the VAPID keypair that `lakko-svc-push-gw`
# uses to encrypt outbound Web Push wakes (RFC 8291). The
# client passes this to `PushManager.subscribe({
# applicationServerKey })` so the browser-side push service
# (FCM endpoint on Chrome, Mozilla autopush on Firefox) binds
# the subscription to *our* server.
#
# Encoded as base64url-no-pad of the 65-byte uncompressed
# P-256 point. Must match the private half on the server
# (`LAKKO_WEBPUSH_VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY_PEM` in the workspace
# `.env`).
#
# Generate once via `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys`:
#
#     $ npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
#     =======================================
#     Public Key:
#     BL...           # ← this value
#
#     Private Key:
#     xZ...           # ← goes in workspace .env
#     =======================================
#
# Unset = the subscribe orchestrator is a no-op (clients
# fall back to foreground polling). Right posture for any
# contributor not actively iterating on push.
# VITE_LAKKO_WEBPUSH_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY_B64URL=
